{"id": "EUVD-2026-82213", "enisaUuid": "e5c952ad-4911-35bd-a7bf-3ac7b7440c95", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nesp: do not unref managed frag pages in esp_ssg_unref()\n\nesp_ssg_unref() releases the page references held on the source\nscatterlist after the AEAD operation completes.  It calls\nskb_page_unref() on every frag page for an out-of-place transform\n(req->src != req->dst), and in the error path of esp_output_tail()\n(already_unref == true) on the request's own scatterlist.\n\nThis is wrong when the skb carries managed frags\n(SKBFL_MANAGED_FRAG_REFS).  Managed frags are owned by a zerocopy ubuf\nand the skb does not hold a per-frag page reference; io_uring SEND_ZC\nwith a registered buffer attaches the bvec pages this way via\nio_sg_from_iter().  The rest of the stack honours this invariant:\nskb_release_data() skips the per-frag unref when SKBFL_MANAGED_FRAG_REFS\nis set, and skb_zcopy_managed() is the guard used at the other unref\nsites.\n\nesp_ssg_unref() is missing that guard, so for a managed-frag skb it\ndrops a page reference the skb never acquired.  This can underflow the\npage reference count and free a page that is still in use.\n\nGuard the function with skb_zcopy_managed() so both unref paths are\nskipped for managed-frag skbs, matching skb_release_data().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:55", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/201bdf10ae92e7cbd524adf8c0323e2a963d5fd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ec55f0c8a6a543cf660584d1346e11f6311ee59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ad6456898f6e6cf58be83bdb607acb1119a9cd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26b6b14c7a0368e317a1e9fb5144ebe6f8d495cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21697720ff43b8dfa25b8e8d9ca7f56f4597fc80"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93105", "GHSA-m483-33mw-4p7w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "136c6598-84d3-3269-8d8a-8eacefb42826", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "39041d5b-13c9-389f-a706-94b80edc57ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac2661c53f35cbe651bef9b07026a5a05ab8ce0 <3ec55f0c8a6a543cf660584d1346e11f6311ee59"}, {"id": "3dc811b1-08de-3251-a029-5e0e167e8977", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac2661c53f35cbe651bef9b07026a5a05ab8ce0 <21697720ff43b8dfa25b8e8d9ca7f56f4597fc80"}, {"id": "76c040f1-40a7-3b8f-ace8-8c2565c854c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "81d421f1-e596-322d-ae66-a5f8a6919064", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "875178f2-9233-3b4c-8263-6002f52bb364", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "890f21f8-f599-34ce-b03e-359b5c036307", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "947ab8e1-c6bc-3031-af5b-b459d45b4315", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac2661c53f35cbe651bef9b07026a5a05ab8ce0 <26b6b14c7a0368e317a1e9fb5144ebe6f8d495cf"}, {"id": "a4094e27-df01-3fb5-a4fa-fd2d19f426fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "b0dc6e1c-da1f-3910-9378-d7348a191dcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac2661c53f35cbe651bef9b07026a5a05ab8ce0 <1ad6456898f6e6cf58be83bdb607acb1119a9cd1"}, {"id": "dc966ebf-fb72-37fd-b91b-d0a0c1a2dd02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cac2661c53f35cbe651bef9b07026a5a05ab8ce0 <201bdf10ae92e7cbd524adf8c0323e2a963d5fd7"}, {"id": "e59e2e2f-2954-3709-9ae2-ba68f